1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,608
Good Morning, Youth Council.

2
00:00:02,608 --> 00:00:03,700
Caroline speaking.

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,471
Oh, hello, I'm interested in standing for election to the Youth Council,

4
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:10,300
and I was told to give you a call.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,188
That's good.

6
00:00:11,188 --> 00:00:13,853
Could I have your name, please?

7
00:00:13,853 --> 00:00:15,630
Yes, it's Roger Brown.

8
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:16,512
Thank you.

9
00:00:16,512 --> 00:00:19,158
I'm Caroline, the Youth Council administrator.

10
00:00:19,158 --> 00:00:24,010
So do you know much about what the Council does, Roger?

11
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:28,450
I've talked to Stephanie - I think she's the chair of the Council.

12
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:29,048
That's right.

13
00:00:29,048 --> 00:00:31,440
And she told me a lot about it.

14
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:35,886
How it's a way for young people to discuss local issues, for example,

15
00:00:35,886 --> 00:00:38,280
and make suggestions to the town council.

16
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:40,253
That's what made me interested.

17
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:40,648
Fine.

18
00:00:40,648 --> 00:00:44,200
Well let me take down some of your details.

19
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,720
First of all, how old are you?

20
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:51,400
You know the Council is for young people aged from 13 to 18?

21
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,173
I've just turned 18.

22
00:00:53,173 --> 00:00:55,833
And where do you live, Roger?

23
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:56,277
Well,

24
00:00:56,277 --> 00:00:58,050
that's a bit complicated.

25
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:01,559
At the moment I'm looking for a flat to rent here,

26
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:06,025
so I'm in a hostel from Monday to Friday, I go back to my

27
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:07,620
parents' place at the weekend.

28
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:08,004
OK,

29
00:01:08,004 --> 00:01:13,000
so where's the best place to send you some information about the Council?

30
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,190
Oh，to my parents' address, please.

31
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:28,450
That's 17, Buckleigh Street-B-U-C-K-L-E-I-G-H Street, Stamford, Lincolnshire,

32
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:31,395
though you don't really need the county.

33
00:01:31,395 --> 00:01:34,760
Oh, I know Stamford - it's a lovely town.

34
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:38,967
And what's the postcode?

35
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:41,070
PE9 7QT

36
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:42,392
Right, thank you.

37
00:01:42,392 --> 00:01:44,596
So are you working here,

38
00:01:44,596 --> 00:01:46,800
or are you a student?

39
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:50,062
I started studying at the university a couple of weeks ago,

40
00:01:50,062 --> 00:01:53,620
and I've got a part-time job for a few hours a week.

41
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,928
What do you do?

42
00:01:54,928 --> 00:01:56,890
Well, I've done several different things.

43
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:59,827
I've just finished a short-term contract as a courier,

44
00:01:59,827 --> 00:02:04,070
and now I'm working as a waiter in one of the big hotels.

45
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:04,429
Uhuh.

46
00:02:04,429 --> 00:02:07,300
That can't leave you much time for studying!

47
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,769
Oh, it's not too bad.

48
00:02:08,769 --> 00:02:10,825
I manage to fit it all in.

49
00:02:10,825 --> 00:02:12,000
What are you studying?

50
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,263
My ambition is to go into parliament eventually,

51
00:02:15,263 --> 00:02:17,710
so my major subject is politics.

52
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:20,677
That's partly why I think the Youth Council is important

53
00:02:20,677 --> 00:02:23,050
and want to be a part of it.

54
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:26,950
And I suppose you've also taking a minor subject, aren't you?

55
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:30,140
I know a lot of people study economics too.

56
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:31,198
I chose history.

57
00:02:31,198 --> 00:02:35,430
To be honest, I'm not finding it as interesting as I expected!

58
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:35,836
OK,

59
00:02:35,836 --> 00:02:42,328
so with your studying and your part-time job, do you have time for any other interests

60
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:43,140
or hobbies?

61
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:48,732
Well, I spend quite a lot of time cycling both around town to get to university

62
00:02:48,732 --> 00:02:49,780
and to work,

63
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:53,310
and also long-distance, from here to London, for instance.

64
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:55,254
That's pretty impressive!

65
00:02:55,254 --> 00:02:56,550
Anything else?

66
00:02:56,550 --> 00:03:00,620
For relaxation I'm also keen on the cinema - I used to go at

67
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:04,690
least once a week，but I can't manage to go so often now.

68
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:05,066
Right.

69
00:03:05,066 --> 00:03:09,200
Are you sure you'll have enough time for the Youth Council?

70
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:12,840
Yes, I've worked out that I can afford to reduce my hours at work,

71
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,400
and that will make the time.

72
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:18,950
So is there any particular aspect of the Youth Council's work that appeals to

73
00:03:18,950 --> 00:03:19,600
you, Roger?

74
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,825
Well my sister is blind,

75
00:03:21,825 --> 00:03:27,165
so I'm particularly interested in working with disabled young people, to try

76
00:03:27,165 --> 00:03:30,280
and improve the quality of their lives.

77
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:30,960
That's great.

78
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,720
Well, the best way to get involved is to be nominated by some people

79
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:36,740
who you know.

80
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:37,069
Right.

81
00:03:37,069 --> 00:03:40,360
Can you tell me how to set about organising that?

82
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,030
You should talk to Jeffrey, our Elections Officer.

83
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:48,422
I can arrange a meeting in the council office with him, if you like.

84
00:03:48,422 --> 00:03:49,050
Yes, please.

85
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:52,720
He'll be here next Monday, if that suits you.

86
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,075
That's the 14th, isn't it?

87
00:03:55,075 --> 00:03:55,545
Yes.

88
00:03:55,545 --> 00:03:57,900
I can manage late afternoon.

89
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:00,700
Would you like to suggest a time?

90
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,100
He generally leaves around 5.30.

91
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:05,174
Well, would 4.30 be OK?

92
00:04:05,174 --> 00:04:07,248
My last class finishes at 4,

93
00:04:07,248 --> 00:04:11,050
so I'd have plenty of time to get to your office.

94
00:04:11,050 --> 00:04:11,419
Right,

95
00:04:11,419 --> 00:04:12,156
that's fine.

96
00:04:12,156 --> 00:04:12,525
Oh,

97
00:04:12,525 --> 00:04:16,950
and could I have a phone number we can contact you on?

98
00:04:16,950 --> 00:04:25,560
Yes, my mobile number's 07788 136711.

99
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,304
Thank you.

100
00:04:26,304 --> 00:04:29,650
Well, well look forward to seeing you next week.

101
00:04:29,650 --> 00:04:31,540
Thanks very much.

102
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:32,170
Goodbye.

103
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:32,800
Bye.
